00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:24.840
Cordon: What?

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.440
Dave: You know, doing some more consumer friendly recipes.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.780
Cordon: No! No! I don't give a crap about that!

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:33.720
What we're cooking comes from a user named HowBizarre.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:34.900
He writes:

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.620
Dave: Cordon. Think about the consequences of that.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:49.700
Cordon: Let's make a bet. I bet I can get you to try some by the end of the episode.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:50.940
Dave: That's not happening.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.720
Cordon: Very well. If you win, I'll make whatever you want, next episode.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.320
But if I win, you have to try a dish of my choosing.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.800
Dave: Fine. Deal. There is literally no way I'm going to try any of that.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:11.200
Cordon: I'll find a way. Afterall... WE ARE THE WOKKING

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.920
DEEEEEADDDDD!!!!

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.760
We are the Wokking Dead!

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:20.960
THE WOKKING DEAD!

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.920
WE ARE THE WOKKING DEAD!!!!!!

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.420
This episode of The Wokking Dead is brought to you by Culinart Productions

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.360
putting the craft in craft services.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.840
First thing you'll need is the right kind of popcorn

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.560
so we're going to go out into the world and do a bit of shopping.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.200
You'll also need plain popcorn

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:23.100
and it's not like Dave needs the extra calories anyways.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.600
You'll also want syrup,

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.420
food coloring,

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:26.040
butter,

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:26.840
sugar,

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:27.900
baking soda,

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:28.680
salt,

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.640
and don't forget my favorite: Pure Vanilla Extract...

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:37.420
You'll also need radioactive material, and what better place to get it, than Japan?

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:41.560
Dave: Cordon, you can't leave the country in the middle of a sh--

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.300
Japan may be known for it's booming cities and majestic temples,

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:50.920
but it is also home to a wonderful black market.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:00.380
I enjoyed my time in Japan, but after 3 weeks paid vacation,

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:05.060
I figured it was time to get back and finish the radioactive popcorn.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:12.780
Dave: Seriously, Cordon, I don't think anybody's going to want to want to eat radioactive popcorn.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.080
I mean, look at this stuff. It looks disgusting.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:19.320
Cordon: SO DO YOU! But you haven't been yanked off the air yet!

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:22.980
Now preheat the oven to 250°.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.980
And use your saucepan, or as I like to use...

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:28.760
WOK!

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:32.520
And put it on medium heat to melt the butter.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.240
Now, pour in some sugar,

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.020
salt,

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:38.420
syrup,

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.440
and stir it in there.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.760
Let it boil for four minutes.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:48.500
Dave: Since we have four minutes, I'd like to talk to you about some regional demographics that we're talk--

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:49.960
Cordon: AUGH, the four minutes is up!

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.980
Ah, OK! Remove from the heat,

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.700
and add food coloring,

00:03:56.860 --> 00:04:00.160
and one shot of vanilla extract.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:02.680
Ahh!

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.180
Yep, there it is.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:09.140
Alright. I like to take a few extra shots of vanilla.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:13.940
Don't use that imitation garbage, or else you won't get your daily dose of alcohol in.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:25.180
That hit the spot!

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.920
After you stir in some baking soda,

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.560
you can coat the popcorn.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:42.320
I like to pretend that I'm pouring searing hot oil all over Dave's face.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.620
Dave: I heard that!

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:49.480
OK. Then pop it in the oven for one human hour.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:55.880
And don't forget to put your radioactive fish on the bottom rack.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:58.820
Now I have to go before--

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.380
Dave: Ugh... Get back here! Cordon...

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:11.180
Oh yeah! Well then I said, "if you want child support, call Dracula!"

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:15.460
Oh, hey. I gotta get back to the show. Later homie!

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:23.400
Ahh! So warm you can feel the radiation poisoning!

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:36.020
The radioactive popcorn is delicious, but I find it's best to just stick one booger in a regular batch of popcorn!

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.220
Why don't you give them a try?

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:04.680
Dave: I will not! I told you, I'm not gonna eat this stuff!

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:06.800
Cordon: Would you eat it with some rice?

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.080
Dave: No, I will not eat it with rice!

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.400
Cordon: Would you eat it with Vincent Price?

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:14.120
Dave: I will NOT eat it with Vincent Price.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:18.540
Cordon: Would you eat it in the back of a sweaty bus filled with hobos?

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.080
Dave: Absolutely not!

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:22.760
Cordon: Toooooo baaaadddd!!!!

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:29.100
Cordon: CZsWorld and Culinart Productions are not responsible if you die from eating this recipe.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:31.300
So what are you waiting for? Eat it!

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:38.320
Dave: Hey! This is actually pretty good.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:40.860
Cordon: That's what I was telling you Dave.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.220
Looks like you forgot about our bet.

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:44.220
Now...

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:47.120
Try this!

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:49.480
Ahh!

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.000
Dave: Eww... what? What is this?

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:56.980
Cordon: Gooseshit!

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:01.720
